    LIGHTING: "Designers mix ambient, task and accent lighting to make a room both useful and atmospheric.",
    LOFT: "An open space with high ceilings, often a converted industrial building with exposed brick and beams.",
    MANTEL: "The shelf above a fireplace, often used to display art, candles and mirrors.",
    MARBLE: "A natural stone with elegant veining, used for counters, floors and tabletops since ancient times.",
    MIDCENTURY: "Mid-century modern: the clean-lined furniture of roughly 1945 to 1970, like the designs of Charles and Ray Eames.",
    MINIMAL: "Minimalism: fewer things, clean surfaces and calm, uncluttered spaces.",
    MIRROR: "A mirror bounces light around and makes a small room feel bigger.",
    MOODBOARD: "A collage of images, colours and materials that captures the look of a design before it’s built.",
    NOOK: "A small, snug corner — a breakfast nook, a reading nook.",
